Stage 5 identifies the decisive defect. The priority `min`/`max` rules replace fixed float folds with total opaque `minVF`/`maxVF`, and the postcondition reuses those same symbols. There is no auxiliary claim or equation connecting them to real extrema. A counter-interpretation that maps them to fresh arbitrary extrema still proves `#Top`; assigning those fresh values 9 and 10 makes the satisfying input `[1.0, 2.0]` denote `[-8.0, -7.0]` instead of Python’s `[0.0, 1.0]`. The exact-comprehension shortcut also lacks the validation skill’s required universal connection theorem, recorded as a separate evidence gap. I’m now running an independent false-postcondition mutation.
Stage 5 completed with an exhaustive 951-record inventory/assessment. The proof-local extrema bridges are rejected as circular result-bearing abstractions; a wrong opaque interpretation still closes, furnishing the required false-conclusion witness.
